# BCIP Project Context

Build a multimodal, culturally grounded batik design-intelligence ecosystem connecting heritage data, color science, explainable AI, and fashion application.

The four user-facing modules are Motif Explorer, Hue Seer, Lasem Guru, and Dress Weaver. Shared modules are Research Lab and Governance Console.

Pilot domain: Batik Lasem. Never assume Batik Lasem meanings or design rules are universal to all batik traditions.

Non-negotiable rules:

1. Never fabricate cultural facts or seed them as real facts. Demo cultural content must be clearly labelled fictional/demo.
2. Every cultural claim needs provenance, scope, confidence, access policy, and review status.
3. Access restrictions apply to database queries, search results, embeddings, AI context, logs, exports, and generated derivatives.
4. Preserve human authorship. Recommendations are editable suggestions, not authoritative design decisions.
5. Distinguish calibrated scientific color analysis from exploratory analysis of ordinary photographs.
6. Build publication-grade reproducibility: dataset version, asset version, algorithm/model version, parameters, prompt/policy version, and timestamps.
